  "reference_no_of_permission_being_relied_on": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The outbuilding for use as a beauty parlour would be inappropriately located in its siting outside of a retail centre which would undermine the vitality and viability of the nearby Enfield Highway Large Local Centre. Insufficient evidence has been submitted to demonstrate the need and rationale for the proposed retail development in this out of centre location and no evidence has been submitted to confirm that the vitality and viability of the Enfield Highway Large Local Centre would not be undermined The development would fail to apply a 'town centre first' approach and contribute towards maintaining the vitality of town centres. The proposal is therefore considered contrary to the NPPF (2024), Policies E2 and T1 of the London Plan 2021; Core Policies 13 and 17 of the Core Strategy 2010 and Policy DMD25 and of the Development Management Document 2014.",
    "The outbuilding for use as a beauty parlour with independent access would be used for purposes that are no longer ancillary to the main dwelling unit. The creation of a separate commercial unit, would result in a development, out of keeping with the pattern and form of development and the character and appearance of the surrounding area, contrary to the NPPF (2024), Policies D4 and D6 of the London Plan (2021); Policy 30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010); Policies DMD6, DMD8, DMD12 and 37 of the Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposal by reason of its siting and the increased activity associated with a separate unit would by reason of the increased noise, disturbance and activity be harmful to the amenities enjoyed by the residents of the neighbouring properties, contrary to the NPPF (2024), Policies D6 and D14 of the London Plan 2021; Core Policies 30 and 32 of the Enfield Core Strategy 2010 and Policies DMD8, DMD12, DMD37 and DMD68 of the Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
